      "edition": "Friday 23 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ranking verdict",
          "heading": "Victor Matfield says Wallabies are 'definitely not top four' after Bledisloe losses",
          "body": "Former Springboks lock Victor Matfield doubts Australia are even a top-five side, and thinks they will not reach the semi-finals of next year's home Rugby World Cup. Asked where the Wallabies sit, his answer was an emphatic no: \"They're definitely not top four. I don't even think top five.\" Australia are seventh on the World Rugby rankings after back-to-back Bledisloe Cup defeats to New Zealand, the first two losses of the Les Kiss era. Ex-All Blacks winger Sir John Kirwan, reviewing the second Bledisloe defeat, said he \"just can't get a read\" on the side."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France recall Gregory Alldritt for November Nations Championship matches",
          "body": ""
