    "465": {
      "date": "2026-10-23",
      "edition": "Friday 23 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching lesson",
          "heading": "Sir Graham Henry says All Blacks learned to train at Test intensity",
          "body": "Former All Blacks coach Sir Graham Henry, now a national selector under Dave Rennie, says the squad's biggest lesson from the South Africa tour is how they train. Players must practise at Test intensity and physicality, a standard that risks injury but is needed to deliver on the weekend, he says. He also cited a Lions fixture in Johannesburg between the first and second Tests as a partial excuse, and admitted the adjustment will take time."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
